<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
Cross-machine HiL (controller.launch.py on Jetson + host.launch.py on desktop) over a direct
Ethernet link, bypassing multicast discovery entirely.

Why: CycloneDDS's default SPDP discovery uses multicast (239.255.0.1), and on a box with more
than one interface the kernel routes that multicast group via whatever has the default route
(`ip route get 239.255.0.1`) -- typically the WiFi interface, not a newly-added direct link, even
after `ip addr add <ip>/24 dev ethX` on both ends. The direct link then carries pings fine
(unicast, has a specific route) but ROS2 nodes on the two machines never discover each other.
Explicit unicast Peers sidesteps that: no multicast route needed, and it's why RTT over the direct
link matters (sub-ms vs 80-330ms measured over WiFi between these two machines).

Use: mount this repo at /ws (as the launch commands already do) and set on the Jetson side
    -e CYCLONEDDS_URI=file:///ws/docker/cyclonedds-jetson.xml
and on the desktop side, docker/cyclonedds-host.xml with the addresses swapped. Update the two
<Peer address> entries below (and the matching file) if the direct-link IPs change.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain>
    <General>
      <NetworkInterfaceAddress>10.10.10.1</NetworkInterfaceAddress>
      <AllowMulticast>false</AllowMulticast>
    </General>
    <Discovery>
      <Peers>
        <Peer address="10.10.10.1"/>
        <Peer address="10.10.10.2"/>
      </Peers>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
